Create a system architecture diagram for a KYC Fraud Detection system called eKS (eSewa KYC Shield) with the following components and connections:

Frontend layer:
- Next.js 16 Frontend (React 19, Tailwind CSS, FingerprintJS)

Orchestration layer:
- Express.js Backend (Node.js) with three route groups: KYC Routes, Admin Routes, Onboarding Routes

ML Services layer (FastAPI Python):
- InsightFace buffalo_l Service (ArcFace 512-dim face embedding + RetinaFace detection)
- Mistral OCR Service (pixtral-12b-2409 vision model, extracts structured fields)
- Forgery Detector Service (6-check pipeline: ELA 47%, EXIF 20%, Font 10%, Noise 10%, Copy-Move 8%, Edge 5%)

Database layer:
- Supabase PostgreSQL with pgvector extension, tables: kyc_submissions, face_embeddings (vector 512), ocr_results, forgery_results, kyc_details

Storage:
- Cloudinary CDN (stores original ID images and cropped face images)

Connections:
- Next.js Frontend sends REST API calls to Express.js Backend
- Express.js Backend calls FastAPI ML Services via HTTP
- FastAPI ML Services read and write to Supabase PostgreSQL
- FastAPI ML Services upload images to Cloudinary
- Express.js Backend also reads from Supabase directly
- InsightFace Service queries face_embeddings table using pgvector cosine similarity for duplicate detection
- Mistral OCR Service writes extracted fields to ocr_results table
- Forgery Detector writes composite score and per-check details to forgery_results table

